# FUSE valgrind suppressions (used by cmake/FuseValgrind.cmake, ctest label "valgrind").
#
# Policy: only THIRD-PARTY / system allocations are suppressed here, each with a comment naming
# the owner and why it is not a FUSE leak. FUSE code is never suppressed: fix the leak instead.
# Regenerate candidates with the --gen-suppressions=all blocks valgrind prints on failure.
#
# Baseline (2026-09, valgrind 3.22, build/fuse-debug): the representative set reports zero
# definitely/indirectly lost blocks and zero memcheck errors without any suppression; the entries
# below cover driver/runtime noise seen when the same binaries run against a Vulkan ICD.

# Mesa lavapipe / llvmpipe (Vulkan software ICD, loaded by RendererBootstrap in
# fuse_runtime_smoke / HybridComposer): a lavapipe rasterizer thread calloc()s 56+56 bytes that
# the ICD never frees (observed in fuse_hybrid_cooked_bindings and fuse_u8_demo_3d_empty). The ICD
# is dlclose()d before the leak scan, so this only matches with --keep-debuginfo=yes (set by
# FuseValgrind.cmake); without it the frames print as ???.
{
   mesa_lavapipe_llvm_jit_caches
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   ...
   obj:*/libvulkan_lvp.so*
}
{
   mesa_llvm_shared_library
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   ...
   obj:*/libLLVM*.so*
}

# Khronos Vulkan loader: layer/ICD manifest JSON parsing caches owned by the loader for the
# process lifetime (freed only by the loader's library destructor).
{
   vulkan_loader_manifest_cache
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   ...
   obj:*/libvulkan.so*
   ...
   fun:vkCreateInstance
}

# glibc dynamic loader: dlopen() of an ICD allocates link-map/TLS bookkeeping that is intentionally
# retained (dlclose of a nodelete library).
{
   glibc_dlopen_linkmap
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   ...
   fun:_dl_open
}
